    "result_text": "The full test suite passes (BUILD SUCCESS). The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI changed the `customerCode` format to `<CITY3>-<LAST3>-<NNNN>` in `OwnerRestControllerV1.java`:\n\n- **`generateCustomerCode`** now takes the city as well as the last name. It builds:\n  - `CITY3` \u2014 upper-cased first three letters of the city\n  - `LAST3` \u2014 upper-cased first three letters of the last name\n  - `NNNN` \u2014 a **per-city** 4-digit zero-padded sequence, computed as one more than the number of existing owners already in that city (previously it was a global count of all owners).\n- Updated the call site in `addOwner` to pass `owner.getCity()`.\n\nEverything derived from `customerCode` rebuilds automatically: the `membershipNumber` in `OwnerMapper` is defined as `owner.getCustomerCode() + \"-M\" + <year>`, so it now carries the new city-prefixed code with no change needed there.\n\nThe acceptance test (which asserts `customerCode` matches `[A-Z]{3}-[A-Z]{3}-\\d{4}`) and the full suite pass with **BUILD SUCCESS**.",
